00:00:02.790 --> 00:00:05.269 align:start position:0%
in east london there is a building it's  known as the cathedral on the marsh but  this is no house of worship  it's a monument to london sewers  [Music]  opened in 1865 the crossness pumping  station was one of the first of its kind  in the world  designed in the romanesque style the  victorian masterpiece was built to  tackle london's struggles with raw  sewage and cholera outbreaks which  killed up to 20 000 people every year  the plant is a testament to beauty in  both form and function almost every inch  is adorned with immaculate ironwork  long pillars support the top floor where  four steam-powered beam engines rest  weighing 47 tons each  the station was part of a system devised  to collect sewage water and discard it  in the eastern part of the city away  from the centre  despite there being other regulations to  reduce sewage at the time the station  has been praised for pushing london into  a healthier less smelly future  as english capital has moved to new  solutions to keep its water clean and  flowing this sewage cathedral is  maintained as a museum showing that even  the dirtiest of jobs can inspire beauty  [Music]  you
 

